   "source": [
    "# Data Preprocessing and Cleaning Notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "**Project:** AI-Based IoT Sensor Anomaly Detection\n",
    "**Phase:** 2 - Data Preprocessing and Cleaning\n",
    "**Datasets:** normal_data.csv, pilot_data.csv, test.csv, test_labels.csv\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Learning Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "In this notebook, you will learn:\n",
    "1. How to load CSV files correctly (with and without headers)\n",
    "2. How to assign column names and convert data types\n",
    "3. How to find and remove exact duplicate rows\n",
    "4. How to handle repeated timestamps with different values\n",
    "4. How to flag suspicious observations without deleting them\n",
    "5. How to convert event-level labels to row-level labels\n",
    "6. How to save processed datasets with clear naming\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Principle:** Never modify original files. Always save processed versions to a separate folder (`data/processed/`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup and Imports\n",
    "\n",
    "We start by importing the libraries we need and setting up our paths."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Pandas version: 3.0.6\n",
      "Data folders ready\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Pandas version:\", pd.__version__)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define our data folders\n",
    "raw_dir = Path(\"data/raw\")\n",
    "processed_dir = Path(\"data/processed\")\n",
    "processed_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Data folders ready\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Load Original Datasets\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Concept: Reading CSV Files\n",
    "\n",
    "- **`pd.read_csv()`** reads a CSV file into a DataFrame\n",
    "- By default, it assumes the **first row is the header** (column names)\n",
    "- If your file has **no header**, use `header=None` and provide names with `names=[...]`\n",
    "- The **original files in `data/raw/` are never modified** — we only read them\n",
    "\n",
    "### Our Files:\n",
    "- `normal_data.csv` — **NO header** (first row is data)\n",
    "- `pilot_data.csv` — HAS header\n",
    "- `test.csv` — HAS header\n",
    "- `test_labels.csv` — HAS header"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "=== NORMAL DATA (no header) ===\n",
