    "print(test_labels)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Convert Data Types\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Concept: Data Types\n",
    "\n",
    "- **`timestamp`** should be **datetime** (not text) so we can do time calculations\n",
    "- **`temperature`** and **`humidity`** should be **float** (decimal numbers)\n",
    "- **`pd.to_datetime()`** converts text timestamps to datetime objects\n",
    "- **`astype(float)`** converts to decimal numbers\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why This Matters:\n",
    "- Datetime allows us to calculate time differences, sort chronologically, and filter by date range\n",
    "- Float allows mathematical operations (mean, std, etc.)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "=== NORMAL DATA TYPES ===\n",
      "timestamp          datetime64[ns]\n",
      "temperature              float64\n",
      "humidity                 float64\n",
      "dtype: object\n",
      "\n",
      "=== PILOT DATA TYPES ===\n",
      "timestamp          datetime64[ns]\n",
      "temperature              float64\n",
      "humidity                 float64\n",
      "dtype: object\n",
      "\n",
      "=== TEST DATA TYPES ===\n",
      "timestamp          datetime64[ns]\n",
      "temperature              float64\n",
      "humidity                 float64\n",
      "dtype: object\n",
      "\n",
      "=== TEST LABELS TYPES ===\n",
      "start          datetime64[ns]\n",
      "end            datetime64[ns]\n",
      "label                 object\n",
      "dtype: object\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Convert timestamps to datetime\n",
    "normal[\"timestamp\"] = pd.to_datetime(normal[\"timestamp\"])\n",
    "pilot[\"timestamp\"] = pd.to_datetime(pilot[\"timestamp\"])\n",
    "test[\"timestamp\"] = pd.to_datetime(test[\"timestamp\"])\n",
    "test_labels[\"start\"] = pd.to_datetime(test_labels[\"start\"])\n",
    "test_labels[\"end\"] = pd.to_datetime(test_labels[\"end\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure temperature and humidity are float\n",
    "normal[\"temperature\"] = normal[\"temperature\"].astype(float)\n",
    "normal[\"humidity\"] = normal[\"humidity\"].astype(float)\n",
    "pilot[\"temperature\"] = pilot[\"temperature\"].astype(float)\n",
    "pilot[\"humidity\"] = pilot[\"humidity\"].astype(float)\n",
    "test[\"temperature\"] = test[\"temperature\"].astype(float)\n",
    "test[\"humidity\"] = test[\"humidity\"].astype(float)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify\n",
    "print(\"=== NORMAL DATA TYPES ===\")\n",
    "print(normal.dtypes)\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== PILOT DATA TYPES ===\")\n",
    "print(pilot.dtypes)\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== TEST DATA TYPES ===\")\n",
    "print(test.dtypes)\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== TEST LABELS TYPES ===\")\n",
    "print(test_labels.dtypes)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Check Missing and Invalid Values\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Concept: Missing Values\n",
    "\n",
    "- **`isnull().sum()`** counts missing (NaN) values in each column\n",
    "- **Invalid values** for temperature/humidity might be: negative humidity, temperature outside sensor range\n",
    "- DHT11 range: Temperature 0-50°C, Humidity 20-90% RH\n",
    "- We **report** invalid values but **don't auto-delete** them"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "=== MISSING VALUES ===\n",
      "Normal data:\n",
