   "source": [
    "### Note on Humidity > 90%\n",
    "\n",
    "- The EDA found humidity values up to 97.2% in normal data\n",
    "- These exceed the DHT11 specification (20-90% RH)\n",
    "- **We do NOT delete these** — they may be real readings in a humid environment, or sensor saturation\n",
    "- We **flag them** for awareness but keep all data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Remove Exact Duplicate Rows (normal_data.csv)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Concept: Exact Duplicates\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Exact duplicate** = all columns have identical values (timestamp, temperature, humidity)\n",
    "- **`df.duplicated()`** returns True for rows that are duplicates of an earlier row\n",
    "- **`df.drop_duplicates(keep=\"first\")`** keeps the first occurrence, removes subsequent duplicates\n",
    "- **We save the removed duplicates** for auditing\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why Remove Exact Duplicates?\n",
    "- They add no new information\n",
    "- They bias the model (same observation counted multiple times)\n",
    "- EDA found **12,776 exact duplicates** in normal_data.csv"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "=== EXACT DUPLICATE ANALYSIS ===\n",
      "Original rows: 49728\n",
      "Exact duplicate rows (all 3 columns): 12776\n",
      "Rows after removing exact duplicates: 36952\n",
      "Duplicates removed: 12776\n",
      "\n",
      "Verification: 36952 + 12776 = 49728 ✓"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Check exact duplicates before removal\n",
    "original_count = len(normal)\n",
    "exact_dup_mask = normal.duplicated(keep=\"first\")  # True for duplicates (not first occurrence)\n",
    "exact_dup_count = exact_dup_mask.sum()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== EXACT DUPLICATE ANALYSIS ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"Original rows: {original_count}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Exact duplicate rows (all 3 columns): {exact_dup_count}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save the duplicate rows for auditing\n",
    "normal_duplicates = normal[exact_dup_mask].copy()\n",
    "normal_duplicates.to_csv(processed_dir / \"normal_data_duplicate_audit.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "print(f\"Duplicate rows saved to: {processed_dir / 'normal_data_duplicate_audit.csv'}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Remove exact duplicates, keep first occurrence\n",
    "normal_dedup = normal.drop_duplicates(keep=\"first\").copy()\n",
    "dedup_count = len(normal_dedup)\n",
    "print(f\"Rows after removing exact duplicates: {dedup_count}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Duplicates removed: {exact_dup_count}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Verification: {dedup_count} + {exact_dup_count} = {dedup_count + exact_dup_count} {'✓' if dedup_count + exact_dup_count == original_count else '✗'}")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Handle Repeated Timestamps with Different Values\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Concept: Duplicate Timestamps\n",
    "\n",
    "- After removing exact duplicates, some timestamps may still appear multiple times\n",
    "- This happens when **timestamp is the same but temperature/humidity differ**\n",
    "- EDA found **304 such rows** (13,065 duplicate timestamps - 12,776 exact duplicates)\n",
    "- **We do NOT auto-delete these** — they may represent real rapid changes or logging race conditions\n",
    "- We **flag them** and keep all rows for now\n",
    "\n",
    "### What We Do:\n",
    "1. Identify timestamps that appear more than once\n",
    "2. Count how many rows per timestamp\n",
    "3. Save a report of these for review\n",
    "4. Keep all rows in the dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "=== REPEATED TIMESTAMPS WITH DIFFERENT VALUES ===\n",
      "Duplicate timestamps (after exact dedup): 304\n",
      "Unique timestamps with duplicates: 14\n",
      "\n",
      "Timestamp                    Count\n",
      "2026-10-30 18:33:40         80\n",
      "2026-10-30 18:36:30         54\n",
      "2026-10-30 18:40:04         53\n",
      "2026-10-30 18:44:56         53\n",
      "2026-10-30 18:49:48         53\n",
      "2026-10-30 18:54:40         53\n",
      "2026-10-30 18:59:32         53\n",
      "2026-10-30 19:04:24         53\n",
      "2026-10-30 19:09:16         53\n",
      "2026-10-30 19:14:08         53\n",
      "2026-10-30 19:19:00         53\n",
      "2026-10-30 19:23:52         53\n",
      "2026-10-30 19:28:44         53\n",
      "2026-10-30 19:33:36         53\n",
      "\n",
      "Report saved to: data/processed/normal_data_repeated_timestamps_report.csv"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Find timestamps that appear more than once in deduplicated data\n",
    "ts_counts = normal_dedup[\"timestamp\"].value_counts()\n",
    "repeated_ts = ts_counts[ts_counts > 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== REPEATED TIMESTAMPS WITH DIFFERENT VALUES ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"Duplicate timestamps (after exact dedup): {repeated_ts.sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Unique timestamps with duplicates: {len(repeated_ts)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show the timestamps and their counts\n",
    "print(\"\\nTimestamp                    Count\")\n",
    "for ts, count in repeated_ts.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"{ts}  {count}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save a detailed report\n",
    "repeated_rows = normal_dedup[normal_dedup[\"timestamp\"].isin(repeated_ts.index)].copy()\n",
    "repeated_rows = repeated_rows.sort_values([\"timestamp\", \"temperature\", \"humidity\"])\n",
    "repeated_rows.to_csv(processed_dir / \"normal_data_repeated_timestamps_report.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nReport saved to: {processed_dir / 'normal_data_repeated_timestamps_report.csv'}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Note: We KEEP all these rows in the dataset\n",
    "# They are flagged for review but not auto-removed"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Investigate Suspicious Tail Observations\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Concept: Verifying EDA Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "- The EDA reported a \"suspicious tail\" with **Temperature = 22.4°C** and **Humidity = 89-92%**\n",
    "- This combination is **physically unusual**: cold air holds less moisture\n",
    "- **We must verify** if these rows actually exist in our data\n",
    "- If they don't exist, the EDA finding was an artifact (possibly from duplicate rows)\n",
    "- **We do NOT auto-delete** — we investigate and report the truth"
   ]
