    "## 10. Prepare Test Dataset with Row-Level Labels\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Concept: Event-Level to Row-Level Labels\n",
    "\n",
    "- **`test_labels.csv`** has **event-level** label: one row marking a time window as \"anomaly\"\n",
    "- **`test.csv`** has **56 rows** of sensor data\n",
    "- We need **row-level labels** (0 = normal, 1 = anomaly) for evaluation\n",
    "- **Method**: For each test row, check if its timestamp falls within the anomaly window\n",
    "- EDA found **10 anomaly rows** (indices 37-46)\n",
    "- We **verify** this count and **report any discrepancy**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "=== TEST DATA PREPARATION ===\n",
      "Test rows: 56\n",
      "Label window: 2026-10-27 22:03:29 to 2026-10-27 22:03:47\n",
      "\n",
      "=== ROW-LEVEL LABEL CREATION ===\n",
      "Rows in anomaly window: 10\n",
      "Rows outside window (normal): 46\n",
      "Label distribution:\n",
      "0    46\n",
      "1    10\n",
      "Name: label, dtype: int64\n",
      "\n",
      "Verification: EDA expected 10 anomaly rows. Match: ✓\n",
      "\n",
      "Saved: data/processed/test_data_with_labels.csv (56 rows)\n",
